\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec5 > What software did you use to create your data visualization?\strokec6 \
	I used python. Specifically the seaborn library.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4     \strokec5 > Who is your intended audience? \strokec6 \
\strokec4     	Policy makers, but also the public\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4     \strokec5 > What information or message are you trying to convey with your visualization? \strokec6 \
\strokec4     	I\'92m trying to make the point that when COVID19 requires ICU care, there is a significant demand for ventilators. This will overburden the healthcare infrastructure\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4     \strokec5 > What aspects of design did you consider when making your visualization? How did you apply them? With what elements of your plots? \strokec6 \
\strokec4     	I wanted to use the stack plot to be able to show the proportional distribution of ICU care based on ventilator use. I thought of using the scatterplot, but it was visually tough to follow along. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4     \strokec5 > How did you ensure that your data visualizations are reproducible? If the tool you used to make your data visualization is not reproducible, how will this impact your data visualization? \strokec6 \
\strokec4     	I used a publicly available and provincially maintained dataset. The data comes directly from the provincial government so it is vetted. Given that I am submitting my code alongside this document, my plot should be reproducible \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4     \strokec5 > How did you ensure that your data visualization is accessible?  \strokec6 \
\strokec4     	I used a colourblind friendly palette\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4     \strokec5 > Who are the individuals and communities who might be impacted by your visualization?  \strokec6 \
\strokec4     	This viz can hopefully make the point that COVID overwhelms ICU infrastructure. If policy makers take action to improve this infrastructure, healthcare providers can serve more patients who are in need, and triage more efficiently without worrying about overwhelming ICU capacity (because there would be more ventilators)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4     \strokec5 > How did you choose which features of your chosen dataset to include or exclude from your visualization? \strokec6 \
\strokec4     	There were several other geographic regions in this dataset. Additionally, the datapoints ranged from 2020-2024. I focused on my own geographic area and used the most recent year as my datapoints. I calculated the # of ICU patients not on ventilation. This was necessary to communicate my point about how burdensome ICU-care of COVID19 patients is on the ICU infrastructure. The stack plot shows that for the majority of the year, patients who are in the ICU for COVID need ventilation. \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
